 "まくをとじる": "[to lower the curtain (at the end of a play)]\nمثال: 記念式典は閉会の辞で幕を閉じた。\n→ The commemorative ceremony ended with the closing address. / فَرَغَ, أَنْهَى (To complete (something).) / اِنْتَهَى (To come to an end.)  [to finish]",
 "まくをひく": "[to draw closed the curtain (of a theatre, etc.)] / فَرَغَ, أَنْهَى (To complete (something).) / اِنْتَهَى (To come to an end.)  [to finish]",
 "まぐさ": "عَلَف (Food for animals; that which is fed to cattle, horses, and sheep, such as hay, c)  [fodder (for horses or cows)]",
 "まぐさおけ": "فِنْطَاس (A long, narrow container, open on top, for feeding or watering animals.)  [trough]",
 "まぐさ桶": "فِنْطَاس (A long, narrow container, open on top, for feeding or watering animals.)  [trough]",
 "まぐち": "عَرْض (The measurement of the extent of something from side to side.)  [width (of a building, plot of land, etc.)]\nمثال: 間口も広いが奥行きも同様に深い。\n→ It's as deep as it is wide. / حَيِّز (The breadth, depth or reach of a subject; the extent of applicability or relevan)  [scope (e.g. of one's work)]",
 "まぐれ": "فُرْصَة (An opportunity or possibility.)  [chance]",
 "まぐろ": "تُونَة, تُنّ (Any of several species of fish of the genus Thunnus in the family Scombridae.)  [tuna (Thunnus spp.; esp. the Pacific bluefin)] / نَجْمَةُ اَلْبَحْرِ (Any of various echinoderms (not in fact fish) with usually five arms, many of wh)  [starfish] / [body of a person struck by a train] / [person unconscious due to alcohol]",
 "まぐろおんな": "نَجْمَةُ اَلْبَحْرِ (Any of various echinoderms (not in fact fish) with usually five arms, many of wh)  [starfish]",
 "まぐわ": "جَرّافَة, كَاسِحَة (A device consisting of a heavy framework having several disks or teeth in a row,)  [harrow]",
 "まぐわい": "جِمَاع, مُجَامَعَة (Sexual interaction, usually involving vaginal, anal, or oral penetration, betwee)  [sexual intercourse] / [communicating love through eye contact ; exchanging looks]",
 "まけ": "غَلَبَ, هَزَمَ (To overcome in battle or contest.) / هَزِيمَة, مَغْلُوبِيَّة (The act or instance of being defeated, of being overcome or vanquished; a loss.)  [defeat]\nمثال: どっちに転んでも君の負けだよ。\n→ Either way, you lose. / [failing to live up to (one's name, looks, etc.)] / خَصْم, تَخْفِيض (A reduction in price.)  [discount]",
 "まけいぬ": "خَاسِر (A person who loses; one who fails to win or thrive.) / فَاشِل (A person who is frequently unsuccessful in life.) / فَاشِل (A contemptible or unfashionable person.)  [loser]\nمثال: 負け犬になるわけにはいかない。\n→ I can't stand getting beaten. / [unmarried and childless older woman]",
 "まけおしみ": "حِصْرِم (Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see sour, grapes.)  [sour grapes]\nمثال: 日本の市場が閉鎖的だという非難は、負け惜しみにすぎません。\n→ Criticisms that Japan's market is closed are just sour grapes.",
 "まけぎらい": "تَنَافُسِيّ (Of or pertaining to competition.)  [competitive]",
 "まけぐみ": "خَاسِر (A person who loses; one who fails to win or thrive.) / فَاشِل (A person who is frequently unsuccessful in life.) / فَاشِل (A contemptible or unfashionable person.)  [losers (of society)]",
 "まけしらず": "مَنِيع (Impossible to defeat, destroy, or kill; too powerful to be defeated or overcome.) / مَنِيع (Someone or something that cannot be defeated, destroyed, or killed.)  [invincible]",
