 "まじ": "جِدِّيّ (Without humor or expression of happiness; grave in manner or disposition.) / جَدِّيّ, جَادّ (Important; weighty; not insignificant.) / جَدِّيّ, جَادّ (Really intending what is said (or planned, etc); in earnest; not jocular or dece)  [serious]\nمثال: 「・・・おい・・・おい、先生！」「え？・・・あ、ああ」「マジだいじょうぶ？休講にしたら？」\n→ \"...Hey...Hey, teacher!\" \"Eh? Oh.\" \"Are you really OK? Shouldn't you cancel the lesson?\"",
 "まじうる": "خَلَطَ, مَزَجَ (To stir together.)  [to mix]\nمثال: その詩は韻文に散文をまじえている。\n→ That poem mixes prose with poetry. / تَبْدِيل, تَبَادُل (An act of exchanging or trading.) / بُورْصَة, تَدَاوُل (A place for conducting trading.) / تَبَادَلَ, صَرَفَ (To trade or barter.)  [to exchange (words, fire, etc.)] / صَلِيب (A geometrical figure consisting of two straight lines or bars intersecting each ) / صَلِيب (A wooden post with a perpendicular beam attached and used (especially in the Rom) / صَلِيب (Alternative letter-case form of Cross (“the Crucifix, the cross on which Christ ) / عَبْر, خِلَال (The cross product of the previous vector and the following vector.) / عَبَرَ (To move relatively.)  [to cross (e.g. swords)]",
