 "まじめ": "جِدِّيّ (Without humor or expression of happiness; grave in manner or disposition.) / جَدِّيّ, جَادّ (Important; weighty; not insignificant.) / جَدِّيّ, جَادّ (Really intending what is said (or planned, etc); in earnest; not jocular or dece)  [serious]\nمثال: サムは仕事に関してまじめです。\n→ Sam is serious about his work. / نَزِيه, صَادِق (Scrupulous with regard to telling the truth; not given to swindling, lying, or f)  [honest]",
 "まじゅつ": "سِحْر (use of rituals or actions exploiting the supernatural) / سِحْرِيّ (Having supernatural talents, properties or qualities attributed to magic.)  [magic]\nمثال: 男は魔術で少女を恐れさせた。\n→ The man awed the girl with his magic tricks. / [magic tricks (with large-scale props)]",
