 "まず": "أَوَّل, أُولَى (Coming right after the zeroth in things that use zero-based numbering.) / أَوَّلاً (Before anything else; firstly.) / أَوَّل (The person or thing in the first position.)  [first (of all)]\nمثال: まず第一に私はジムを訪ねなければならない。\n→ First of all, I have to call on Jim. / مِن اَلْمُحْتَمَل, رُبَّمَا (In all likelihood.)  [probably]\nمثال: あのチームは、あるとしても、まず優勝の望みはない。\n→ That team has little, if any, chance of winning. / حَوَالِي (Approximately.)  [more or less (satisfactory)] / عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]",
 "まずしい": "فَقِير (With no or few possessions or money, particularly in relation to contemporaries ) / مِسْكِين (Worthy of pity.) / فُقَرَاء (The poor people of a society or the world collectively, the poor class of a soci)  [poor]\nمثال: われわれは貧しい人あざ笑ってはいけない。\n→ We must not laugh at the poor. / نَقْص, عَدَم وُجُود (A deficiency or need (of something desirable or necessary); an absence, want, de)  [lacking (quantity and quality-wise)]",
 "まずだいいちに": "أَوَّلًا, قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ (Firstly; before anything else.)  [first of all]\nمثال: まず第一にここにお招きいただいてとても嬉しく思っている事を述べます。\n→ First of all, let me say how glad I am to be here.",
 "まずない": "نَادِرًا (Infrequently, rarely.)  [seldom]\nمثال: 彼は映画館に行くことはまずない。\n→ He seldom, if ever, goes to the cinema.",
 "まずは": "أَوَّلًا, قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ (Firstly; before anything else.)  [first of all]\nmore emphatic than まず\nمثال: まずは公式を暗記しなさい。\n→ First of all, learn the formula by heart. / مِن اَلْمُحْتَمَل, رُبَّمَا (In all likelihood.)  [probably] / حَوَالِي (Approximately.)  [more or less (satisfactory)] / عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]",
 "まずまず": "كَافٍ (Equal to or fulfilling some requirement.)  [adequate]\nمثال: 彼の仕事はまずまずの出来だが、とても優秀とは言えなかった。\n→ His work was acceptable, but far from excellent.",
 "まずもって": "أَوَّلًا, قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ (Firstly; before anything else.)  [first of all]",
 "まず無い": "نَادِرًا (Infrequently, rarely.)  [seldom]\nمثال: 彼は映画館に行くことはまずない。\n→ He seldom, if ever, goes to the cinema.",
 "まず第一に": "أَوَّلًا, قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ (Firstly; before anything else.)  [first of all]\nمثال: まず第一にここにお招きいただいてとても嬉しく思っている事を述べます。\n→ First of all, let me say how glad I am to be here.",
 "ませ": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nimperative form of ～ます; attaches to the -masu stem of an honorific verb; used to make a polite request or demand / [used to increase the politeness of a greeting]",
 "ません": "لَا, مَا (Negates the meaning of the modified verb.) / لَا (And not.)  [not]\nafter the -masu stem of a verb; forms the polite negative non-past tense",
 "まぜあわす": "مُرَكَّب (Composed of elements; not simple.)  [to compound]\nمثال: 彼女はバターと砂糖を混ぜ合わせた。\n→ She mixed the butter and sugar together.",
