 "またぬの": "سَرْج, سرج (A seat for a rider, typically made of leather and raised in the front and rear, )  [saddle]",
 "またね": "إِلَى اللِّقَاء (short for goodbye — see also goodbye) / مَعَ السَّلَامَة (short for goodbye — see also goodbye) / سَلَام (short for goodbye — see also goodbye)  [bye]",
 "または": "أَو, أَم (An operator denoting the disjunction of two propositions or truth values. There )  [or]\nمثال: 紅茶またはコーヒーはいかが？\n→ Would you like some tea or coffee?",
 "またまた": "مَرَّة أُخْرَى (Again, once more, one more time.)  [once again]\nمثال: またまた彼らはけんかをしているようです。\n→ It looks like they are at it again.",
 "またも": "مَرَّة أُخْرَى (Another time: indicating a repeat of an action.)  [(once) again]\nمثال: かわいそうな事にその老いた女性はまたもバッグを盗まれた。\n→ The poor old woman had her bag stolen again.",
 "またもや": "مَرَّة أُخْرَى (Again, once more, one more time.)  [once again]\nمثال: あなたの行いはまたもや厄介なことを引き起こした。\n→ Your conduct gave rise to another problem.",
 "またーり": "غَنِيّ (having wealth)  [rich (taste)] / اِسْتَرْخَى (To become loose.)  [relaxed]",
 "また上": "خَصْر, وَسَط (The part of the body between the pelvis and the stomach.)  [waist (the part of the pants located above the crotch)]",
 "また抜き": "جِسْرٌ صَغِير (The playing of the ball between the legs of an opponent.)  [nutmeg (in soccer)]",
 "また明日": "أَرَاكَ غَدًا (Used as a farewell, stating that the speaker and interlocutor(s) will see each o)  [see you tomorrow]\nمثال: それじゃまた明日。\n→ See you tomorrow.",
 "まだ": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]\nمثال: まだ肉眼じゃ無理だよ。双眼鏡だと、ちょびっとだけ見えるかも・・・。\n→ It's still impossible with the naked eye. With binoculars you might be able to glimpse it.... / بَعْد (Not as of the time referenced.)  [(not) yet]\nwith verb in the negative\nمثال: 私はまだその問題が解けない。\n→ I haven't been able to solve the problem yet. / أَكْثَر (comparative degree of many: in greater number. (Used for a discrete quantity.)) / أَكْثَر (comparative degree of much: in greater quantity, amount, or proportion. (Used fo) / أَكْثَر (comparative of much)  [more] / عَلَى اَلْأَقَلّ (At a minimum or lower limit.) / عَلَى الأَقَلِّ (In any event; anyway.)  [at least]\nمثال: 情報がないより悪い知らせでもあるほうがまだましだ。\n→ Bad news is preferable to an absence of information.",
 "まだしも": "بِالْأَحْرَى (Used to specify a choice or preference; preferably, in preference to. (Now usual)  [rather]\nمثال: この方がまだしもあれよりよい。\n→ This would be better than that.",
 "まだたき": "رَمَشَ (to close and reopen both eyes quickly) / رَمْشَة (The act of quickly closing both eyes and opening them again.)  [blink (of eyes)]\nمثال: 彼女はまばたきして涙を止めようとした。\n→ She blinked to stop the tears. / لَأْلَأَ (To shine with a flickering light; to glimmer.)  [twinkling (of stars)]",
 "まだたく": "لَأْلَأَ (To shine with a flickering light; to glimmer.)  [to twinkle (e.g. stars)]\nمثال: 星が空に瞬いていた。\n→ The stars were twinkling in the sky. / رَمَشَ (to close and reopen both eyes quickly) / رَمْشَة (The act of quickly closing both eyes and opening them again.)  [to blink (one's eyes)]\nまたたく is sometimes used transitively",
 "まだまだ": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]\nmore emphatic than まだ\nمثال: いずれどこかに落ち着いて身を固めるつもりだが、まだまだだ。\n→ Eventually I'd like to settle down and have a family, but not yet. / [still a long way to go ; still a long way off]\nas 〜だ, 〜です, etc.",
 "まだら": "بُقْعَة (A round or irregular patch on the surface of a thing having a different color, t)  [spots]\nمثال: 赤白まだらのタオルを一本ください。\n→ A red and spotted white towel, please. / مُنَقَّط, أَرْقَط (Discoloured by spots; stained.) / أَبْرَش (Characterized by spots (used especially of animals and plants).)  [spotted]",
 "まだらうま": "حِمَار وَحْشِيّ, حِمَار وَحْشِيّ مُخَطَّط (A biracial person, specifically one born to a Sub-Saharan African person and a w)  [zebra]",
 "まだるい": "بَطِيء (Taking a long time to move or go a short distance, or to perform an action; not ) / أَبْطَأَ, بَطَّأَ (To make (something) run, move, etc. less quickly; to reduce the speed of.)  [(frustratingly) slow]",
 "まだるっこい": "بَطِيء (Taking a long time to move or go a short distance, or to perform an action; not ) / أَبْطَأَ, بَطَّأَ (To make (something) run, move, etc. less quickly; to reduce the speed of.)  [(frustratingly) slow]",
 "まだるっこしい": "بَطِيء (Taking a long time to move or go a short distance, or to perform an action; not ) / أَبْطَأَ, بَطَّأَ (To make (something) run, move, etc. less quickly; to reduce the speed of.)  [(frustratingly) slow]",
 "まち": "مَدِينَة, قَرْيَة (A settlement; an area with residential districts, shops and amenities, and its o)  [town]\nesp. 町\nمثال: 町が一面すっぽり雪をかぶった。\n→ Snow completely covered the town. / وَسَطُ البَلَد (The main business part of a city or town, usually located at or near its center.)  [downtown]\nمثال: 楽隊が町をパレードした。\n→ The band paraded the streets. / شَارِع, زَنَقَة (A paved part of road, usually in a village or a town.)  [street]",
 "まちあい": "اِجْتِمَاع, مَجْلِس (A gathering of persons for a purpose; an assembly.) / مُلَاقَاة, مُقَابَلَة (An encounter between people, even accidental.) / مُلَاقَاة, لِقَاء (An administrative unit in the Religious Society of Friends (Quakers).)  [meeting] / [area where guests gather before the start of a tea ceremony] / غُرْفَةُ الاِنْتِظَار (A room in a public place for people to wait.)  [waiting room] / [meeting place for assignations, drinking, etc.]",
 "まちあいしつ": "غُرْفَةُ الاِنْتِظَار (A room in a public place for people to wait.)  [waiting room]\nمثال: 彼は待合室に座っています。\n→ He's sitting in the waiting room.",
 "まちあいじょ": "مَلَاذ (a refuge or other protection) / مَخْلَص (a refuge or other protection)  [shelter (for buses)] / غُرْفَةُ الاِنْتِظَار (A room in a public place for people to wait.)  [waiting room]",
 "まちあわせ": "مَوْعِد, مِيعَاد (An arrangement between people to meet; an engagement.)  [appointment]\nمثال: 何時にどこで待ち合わせする？\n→ What time and where could we meet?",
 "まちうけ": "اِنْتَظَرَ (To delay movement or action until some event or time; to remain neglected or in )  [waiting (for)] / وَرَق حَائِط, خَلْفِيَّة (Decorative paper-like material used to cover the inner walls of buildings.)  [(phone) wallpaper]",
 "まちうけがぞう": "وَرَق حَائِط, خَلْفِيَّة (Decorative paper-like material used to cover the inner walls of buildings.)  [(phone) wallpaper]",
 "まちうけがめん": "وَرَق حَائِط, خَلْفِيَّة (Decorative paper-like material used to cover the inner walls of buildings.)  [(phone) wallpaper]",
 "まちうける": "اِنْتَظَرَ, اِسْتَأْنَى (To wait for.)  [to await]\nمثال: どの進路を選んでも危険が待ち受けている。\n→ Whichever way we choose will involve danger.",
 "まちかご": "حَمَّالَة, مِحَفَّة (An enclosed human-borne litter or sedan chair, a large box with a chair, couch, )  [palanquin]",
 "まちかた": "مَدِينَة, قَرْيَة (A settlement; an area with residential districts, shops and amenities, and its o)  [town]",
 "まちかど": "زاوِيَةِ, نَاصِيَة (The corner of a street, usually where two streets meet at an intersection.)  [street corner]\nمثال: あの町かどに公衆電話ボックスがある。\n→ There is a telephone booth at the corner of the street.",
 "まちかまえる": "اِنْتَظَرَ (To delay movement or action until some event or time; to remain neglected or in )  [to wait (for)]\nمثال: 私は最後のチャンスを待ち構えた。\n→ I watched for the last chance.",
 "まちが": "وَرَق حَائِط, خَلْفِيَّة (Decorative paper-like material used to cover the inner walls of buildings.)  [(phone) wallpaper]",
 "まちがい": "أَسَاء اَلْفَهْم, أَخْطَأَ (To understand wrongly, taking one thing or person for another.) / خَطَأ, غَلْطَة (An error.)  [mistake]\nمثال: この本は間違いだらけだ。\n→ This book is full of mistakes. / حَادِث (A collision or crash of a vehicle, aircraft, or other form of transportation tha) / مُصَادَفَة, صُدْفَة (Any chance event.) / صُدْفَة, صِدْفَة (Chance; random chance.)  [accident] / [improper conduct (e.g. between man and woman) ; indiscretion]",
 "まちがいでんわ": "رَقْم غَيْر صَحِيح (A call with a mistake in the number dialled) / رَقْم خَاطِئ (A call with a mistake in the number dialled)  [wrong number]",
 "まちがいない": "أَكِيد (sure, positive, not doubting) / مُتَأَكِّد (sure, positive, not doubting) / بَعْض (not specifically named, indeterminate, indefinite) / مُحَدَّد (Having been determined but not specified.)  [certain]\nمثال: この列車に間違いないですか。\n→ Are you sure this is the right train? / مَوْثُوق (Suitable or fit to be relied on; worthy of dependence, reliance or trust; depend)  [reliable]",
 "まちがいなく": "بِالتَّأْكِيد (In a way which is certain; with certainty.) / بِالتَّأْكِيد, بِدُون شَكّ (Without doubt, surely.) / بِالتَّأْكِيد, بِدُون شَكّ (An emphatic affirmative answer; of course.)  [certainly]\nمثال: それは間違いなく空飛ぶ円盤だったのだ。\n→ It was a flying saucer all right.",
 "まちがいなし": "أَكِيد (sure, positive, not doubting) / مُتَأَكِّد (sure, positive, not doubting) / بَعْض (not specifically named, indeterminate, indefinite) / مُحَدَّد (Having been determined but not specified.)  [certain]\nمثال: 毎日大食していると、ブクブク太り過ぎること間違いなし。\n→ If you pig out every day, you're sure to gain too much weight.",
 "まちがう": "[to be mistaken ; to be incorrect]\nas 間違っている or 間違った\nمثال: 彼女の名前のつづりが間違っていた。\n→ Her name was spelled wrong. / أَخْطَأَ (To err, to be wrong. (This entry is a translation hub.))  [to make a mistake (in)]\nمثال: 番号を間違っていると思います。\n→ I think you have the wrong number. / أَسَاء اَلْفَهْم, أَخْطَأَ (To understand wrongly, taking one thing or person for another.) / خَطَأ, غَلْطَة (An error.)  [to mistake (one thing with another)]\nمثال: 彼はとても若く見えるのでよく学生と間違われる。\n→ He is often taken for a student because he looks so young.",
 "まちがえ": "أَسَاء اَلْفَهْم, أَخْطَأَ (To understand wrongly, taking one thing or person for another.) / خَطَأ, غَلْطَة (An error.)  [mistake]\nمثال: お間違えではないでしょうか。\n→ I'm afraid you have the wrong number. / حَادِث (A collision or crash of a vehicle, aircraft, or other form of transportation tha) / مُصَادَفَة, صُدْفَة (Any chance event.) / صُدْفَة, صِدْفَة (Chance; random chance.)  [accident] / [improper conduct (e.g. between man and woman) ; indiscretion]",
 "まちがえでんわ": "رَقْم غَيْر صَحِيح (A call with a mistake in the number dialled) / رَقْم خَاطِئ (A call with a mistake in the number dialled)  [wrong number]\nمثال: あらごめんなさい。どうやら間違え電話をしてしまったようだね。\n→ Oh, I'm sorry. I guess I have the wrong number.",
 "まちがえる": "أَخْطَأَ (To err, to be wrong. (This entry is a translation hub.))  [to make a mistake (in)]\nمثال: 彼は答えを三つ間違えた。\n→ He gave three wrong answers. / أَسَاء اَلْفَهْم, أَخْطَأَ (To understand wrongly, taking one thing or person for another.) / خَطَأ, غَلْطَة (An error.)  [to mistake (one thing for another)]\nمثال: 彼女は砂糖を塩と間違えた。\n→ She mistook the sugar for salt.",
