 "まぬがれる": "هَرَبَ (To get free; to free oneself.) / فِرَار, هُرُوب (The act of leaving a dangerous or unpleasant situation.)  [to escape (disaster, death, etc.)]\nمثال: われわれはかろうじて事故を免れた。\n→ We narrowly missed the accident. / تَجَنَّبَ (To keep away from; to keep clear of; to stay away from.)  [to avoid (e.g. punishment)]",
 "まぬけ": "غَبِيّ (Without intelligence.) / غَبِيّ, أَحْمَق (A stupid person; a fool.)  [stupid]\nمثال: あいつはクラスでいちばんのまぬけだ。\n→ He is the dumbest kid in the class. / مُغَفَّل, أَحْمَق (A person with poor judgment or little intelligence.)  [fool]",
 "まね": "قَلَّدَ (To follow as a model or a pattern; to make a copy, counterpart or semblance of.)  [imitating]\nمثال: その少年は馬鹿なまねをした。\n→ The boy made a fool of himself. / سُلُوك, تَصَرُّف (The way or manner a living creature behaves or acts generally.)  [behavior]",
 "まねき": "دَعْوَة, عزيمة (The act of inviting; solicitation; the requesting of a person's company.) / إِغْرَاء (Allurement; enticement.)  [invitation]\nمثال: お招き下さってありがとうございました。\n→ It was kind of you to invite us.",
