 "まるで": "كَأَنَّ, كَأَنَّمَا (As though; in a manner suggesting.)  [as if]\nusu. followed by a form of ようだ or みたいだ\nمثال: まるで夢を見ているようだよ。\n→ I feel as if I were dreaming. / أبداً (Indicating degree, quantity or frequency greater than zero: to the slightest deg)  [(not) at all]\nwith neg. sentence\nمثال: ぼくにはまるでその理由がわからない。\n→ I have no idea why it is so. / حَقًّا (Actually; in fact; in reality.) / وَٱللّٰه؟ (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / لَيْسَ مَعْقُل! (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / حَقًّا (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some )  [really]\nمثال: 彼は私をまるで他人行儀に扱う。\n→ He treats me as if I am a stranger.",
