 "みなり": "لَبِسَ (intransitive: to put on clothes — see also get dressed, wear) / ثَوْب, لِبَاس (An item of clothing (usually worn by a woman or young girl) which both covers th) / كَسْوَة, مَلْبَس (Apparel or clothing, especially when appropriate for a particular occasion, prof)  [dress]\nمثال: こんな身なりで外出するのは気が引ける。\n→ I'm ashamed to go out dressed like this.",
 "みなわ": "رَغْوَة (substance composed of a large collection of bubbles or their) / زَبَد (substance composed of a large collection of bubbles or their) / زَبَد البَحْر (substance composed of a large collection of bubbles or their)  [foam] / لَا شَيْء (Not any thing; no thing.)  [nothing]",
 "みにいく": "زَارَ (To go and meet (a person) as an act of friendliness or sociability.) / زِيَارَة (A single act of visiting.)  [to visit]\nمثال: 映画を見に行きませんか。\n→ How about going to the movies?",
 "みにおぼえのある": "مَأْلُوف (Known to one, or generally known; commonplace.)  [familiar (to one)]\nمثال: だれか身に覚えのある人がいるんじゃないか。\n→ There's somebody here who did it, isn't there?",
 "みにくい": "قَبِيح, بَشِع (Displeasing to the eye; aesthetically unpleasing.)  [ugly]\nمثال: 「美しい」とか「醜い」といった言葉は相対的な用語である。\n→ The words 'beautiful' and 'ugly' are relative terms. / [unsightly ; unseemly]\nمثال: オレの醜い部分がオレを引き裂く。\n→ The ugly side of myself tears me up.",
 "みにくいあひるのこ": "بَطَّة قَبِيحَة (A young person who is ugly, but who is expected to become beautiful or handsome )  [ugly duckling]",
 "みにくいあひるの子": "بَطَّة قَبِيحَة (A young person who is ugly, but who is expected to become beautiful or handsome )  [ugly duckling]",
 "みにくいアヒルの子": "بَطَّة قَبِيحَة (A young person who is ugly, but who is expected to become beautiful or handsome )  [ugly duckling]",
 "みにくる": "زَارَ (To go and meet (a person) as an act of friendliness or sociability.) / زِيَارَة (A single act of visiting.)  [to visit]\nمثال: キャシーが今夜、私達の赤ちゃんを見に来る。\n→ Cathy is coming to see our baby tonight.",
 "みにつく": "سَيِّد (Someone who has control over something or someone.) / سَيِّد (The owner of an animal or slave.) / أُصُولِيّ, أُصُولِيَّة (An expert at something.) / أحسن, أتقن (To learn to a high degree of proficiency.)  [to master (e.g. a skill)]\nمثال: 毎日一生懸命に英語を勉強したが、あまり身につかなかった。\n→ I studied English very hard every day, but I didn't learn a lot. / أَبْقَى (to keep (something) in control or possession; to continue ha) / أَدَامَ (to keep (something) in control or possession; to continue ha) / بَقَّى (to keep (something) in control or possession; to continue ha) / حَفِظَ (to keep (something) in control or possession; to continue ha) / رَعَى (to keep (something) in control or possession; to continue ha) / صانَ (to keep (something) in control or possession; to continue ha)  [to retain]",
 "みにつける": "تَعَلَّمَ (To acquire, or attempt to acquire knowledge or an ability to do something.) / تَعَلَّمَ (To attend a course or other educational activity.) / اِعْتَبَرَ, اِتَّعَظَ (To gain knowledge from a bad experience so as to improve.)  [to learn]\nesp. 身に付ける\nمثال: 「日本の経営陣は米国の労働者の扱い方を身につけなければいけない」と彼は言った。\n→ Japanese management must learn how to deal with American workers, he said. / حَمَلَ (To lift (something) and take it to another place; to transport (something) by li)  [to carry]\nesp. 身に着ける\nمثال: ダイヤの指輪なんて身につけていないけど、私は幸せだ。\n→ I'm not wearing a diamond ring, but I'm happy.",
 "みにでかける": "حَضَرَ ((''ambitransitive'') to be present at or regularly go to)  [to attend (e.g. game, performance)]\nمثال: 何百万の人が実際に自分で見に出かけるとき以上の数のゲームを見ることが出来る。\n→ Millions of people can see more games than when they have to attend each one in person.",
 "みにまとう": "لَبِسَ (to have on (clothes or accessories)) / اِرْتَدَى (to have on (clothes or accessories)) / اِهْتِراء (Damage to the appearance and/or strength of an item caused by use over time.)  [to wear]",
 "みにゅうりょく": "خَالٍ, اَلْخَالِي (Free from writing, printing, or marks; having an empty space to be filled in.)  [blank]",
 "みぬく": "أَدْرَكَ, وَعَى (To become aware of, through the physical senses, to see; to understand.)  [to perceive]\nمثال: 私は彼らの陰謀をすぐに見抜いた。\n→ I saw through their plot at once.",
 "みね": "أَوْجٌ, ذُرْوَةٌ (The highest value reached by some quantity in a time period.)  [peak]\nمثال: その峰は雲の上にそびえている。\n→ The peak rises above the clouds. / [back of a blade]",
 "みねみね": "أَوْجٌ, ذُرْوَةٌ (The highest value reached by some quantity in a time period.)  [peaks]",
 "みのある": "صُلْب (in the solid state) / جَامِد (in the solid state)  [solid]\nمثال: 実のある勉強をしたので、彼の平均点は驚くほど上がりました。\n→ After doing quality work, his average has gone up marvellously.",
 "みのがし": "صَفَحَ (To pretend not to have noticed (something, especially a mistake or flaw); to pas)  [overlooking]\nمثال: その建物は右側にあります。見逃しっこありません。\n→ The building is on your right. You can't miss it. / [letting a good ball go by]",
 "みのがす": "أَخْطَأَ (To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.) / فَاتَ (To fail to experience, attend, partake, take advantage of, etc.) / اِفْتَقَدَ, اِشْتَاقَ (To become aware of the loss or absence of; to feel the want or need of, sometime) / آنِسَة (An unmarried woman; a girl.)  [to miss]\nمثال: これは絶対見逃せないよ。\n→ It's just too good to pass up. / صَفَحَ (To pretend not to have noticed (something, especially a mistake or flaw); to pas)  [to overlook (e.g. a wrongdoing)] / [to pass up (e.g. an opportunity)] / [to let (a good ball) go by]",
 "みのけのよだつ": "رَهِيب, فَظِيع (Causing horror; terrible; shocking.) / فَظِيع, أَرْبَد (Tremendously bad.)  [horrible]\nمثال: それは身の毛のよだつ思いだよ。\n→ That's a hair-raising thought.",
 "みのこなし": "عَرَبَة (A (mostly four-wheeled) lighter vehicle chiefly designed to transport people, ge)  [carriage]\nمثال: ファッションモデルは身のこなしがよくなければならない。\n→ A fashion model must have a good carriage.",
