 "もうしでる": "اِقْتِرَاح (A proposal that has been made.) / اِقْتَرَحَ, قَدَّمَ (To propose or express one's willingness (to do something).) / قَدَّمَ (To present (something) to God or gods, as a gesture of worship or as a sacrifice)  [to offer]\nمثال: 私は彼女にお金を貸そうと申し出た。\n→ I offered to lend money to her.",
 "もうしのべる": "وَضْع (A condition; a set of circumstances applying at any given time.) / دَوْلَة (A polity or community.) / وِلَايَة (A polity or community.) / يُبْدِي (To make known.)  [to state]",
 "もうしひらき": "عَذَرَ (To forgive; to pardon; to overlook.) / اِعْتَذَرَ (To allow to leave, or release from any obligation.) / عُذْر (An explanation designed to avoid or alleviate guilt or negative judgment; a plea)  [excuse]\nمثال: 君は自分の行動の申し開きをしなければならない。\n→ You must account for your conduct.",
 "もうしひらく": "شَرَحَ (to make intelligible) / فَسَّرَ (to make intelligible) / أَبَانَ (to make intelligible)  [to explain]",
 "もうしぶん": "شِكَايَة, شَكْوَى (A grievance, problem, difficulty, or concern.)  [complaint]\nwith neg. sentence\nمثال: その人が申し分がないからといって、恋に落ちるわけではない。\n→ You don't fall in love with somebody because he's perfect. / دَعْوَى, اِدِّعَاء (A new statement of something one believes to be the truth, usually when the stat) / مُطَالَبَة (A legal demand for compensation or damages.) / ٱِدَّعَى, زَعَمَ (To state a new fact, typically without providing evidence to prove it is true.)  [claim]",
 "もうしぶんない": "كَامِل (Fitting its definition precisely.) / كَامِل (Having all of its parts in harmony with a common purpose.) / أَتْقَنَ (To make perfect; to improve or hone.)  [perfect]\nمثال: 今のところはすべて申し分無い。\n→ Everything is fine so far.",
