 "もうしゃ": "مَكْفوف  [blind person]",
 "もうしょ": "مَوْجَة اَلْحَرّ (period of very hot weather)  [heat wave]\nمثال: 猛暑をどうしのいでいますか。\n→ How are you keeping off this intense heat?",
 "もうしよう": "كَلِمَة, كَلَام (Something that someone said; a comment, utterance; speech.) / كَلِمَةُ اللهِ (Communication from God; the message of the Christian gospel; the Bible, Scriptur)  [words]",
 "もうしわけ": "اِعْتِذَار, عُذْر (An expression of remorse or regret for having said or done something that harmed) / دِفَاع, تَبْرِير (A formal justification, defence.)  [apology]",
 "もうしわけありません": "أَنَا آسِف, أَنَا آسِفَة (Indicates that the speaker is confused or requests information to be repeated; c)  [I'm sorry]\nمثال: 申し訳ありませんが、満席です。\n→ I'm sorry, the flight is full. / شُكْرًا جَزِيلًا, أَلْف شُكْر (Said to express greater gratitude than would be conveyed by thank you.)  [thank you very much (for help, etc.)]\nمثال: ご迷惑をおかけして、本当に申し訳ありません。\n→ I really appreciate all the trouble you've gone to.",
