 "もたもた": "بِبُطْء (At a slow pace.)  [slowly]\nمثال: も〜う、モタモタしないの。遅刻になっちゃうでしょ。ほら、紐、結んであげる。\n→ Oooh, get a move on. We'll end up late! Come on, I'll tie your shoelaces for you.",
 "もたらす": "أَحْضَرَ, جَاءَ بِـ (To transport toward somebody/somewhere.)  [to bring (news, knowledge, etc.)]\nمثال: 多くのものが中国から日本にもたらされた。\n→ Many things were brought to Japan from China. / قَضِيَّة (A goal, aim or principle, especially one which transcends purely selfish ends.) / سَبَّبَ (To set off an event or action; to bring about; to produce.)  [to cause]\nمثال: 科学は私達の生活に多くの変化をもたらした。\n→ Science has brought about many changes to our lives.",
 "もたれかかる": "مَالَ (To incline, deviate, or bend, from a vertical position; to be in a position thus) / اِسْتَنَدَ, اِتَّكَأَ (To rest or rely, for support, comfort, to use as a hard surface for writing, etc)  [to lean (on, against)]\nمثال: 彼は壁にもたれかかっていた。\n→ He was leaning against the wall. / [to rely on (someone) ; to depend on]",
 "もだえ": "أَلَم (Extreme pain or anguish.) / اِحْتِضَار (The last struggle of life; death struggle.)  [agony]",
