 "もちあう": "رَصِيد (A list accounting for the debits on one side, and for the credits on the other.)  [to balance] / [to remain unchanged] / نَصِيب, حِصَّة (A portion of something, especially a portion given or allotted to someone.) / سَهْم (A financial instrument that shows that one owns a part of a company that provide) / شَارَكَ (To give part of what one has to somebody else to use or consume.) / شَارَكَ (To divide and distribute.)  [to share (e.g. the expense)]",
 "もちあがる": "نَهَضَ, اِرْتَفْعَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.) / أَشْرَقَ, شَرَقَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.)  [to rise]\nمثال: この机は重くて持ち上がらなかった。\n→ This desk was too heavy to lift. / حَدَثَ, وَقَعَ (To happen or take place.)  [to occur]\nمثال: 株価上昇を契機に新工場建設の話が持ち上がった。\n→ They took advantage of the stock price increase to raise the idea of building a new factory. / [to be homeroom teacher for the same class multiple years in a row ; to move up with one's class]",
 "もちあげる": "رفع (raise)  [to elevate]\nمثال: この石は重すぎて持ち上げられない。\n→ This stone is too heavy to lift. / تَمَلَّقَ, تَبَصْبَصَ (To compliment someone, often (but not necessarily) insincerely and sometimes to )  [to flatter]",
